12. If the selected card doesn't match any card on the table, the players' card gets added to the existing cards on the table.
13. When a player has no cards left on his hand, he receives three new cards from the deck.
14. Once all the cards have been distributed to the players, the round comes to an end. If there are any cards left on the table, the player who last drew cards could take them on his discard pile.
15. After the round has ended, all players tally up their points. If any player reaches the predetermined score, the game ends.
16. At the end of each round, the players receive a reasonable amount of points for each of the following rules applied to the discard piles of each player: the player with the most cards, the player with the most coins cards, the player who has the seven of Coins, the player with the highest sum of their cards.

